{"key":"enterprise/T1547.010","id":"T1547.010","name":"Port Monitors","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1547","tactics":["persistence","privilege-escalation"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may use port monitors to run an adversary supplied DLL during system boot for persistence or privilege escalation. A port monitor can be set through the AddMonitor API call to set a DLL to be loaded at startup. This DLL can be located in C:\\Windows\\System32 and will be loaded and run by the print spooler service, `spoolsv.exe`, under SYSTEM level permissions on boot. Alternatively, an arbitrary DLL can be loaded if permissions allow…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1547/010","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--43881e51-ac74-445b-b4c6-f9f9e9bf23fe","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:42.872Z","source_object_version":"1.3","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0021","name":"OS API Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0021","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9bde2f9d-a695-4344-bfac-f2dce13d121e","page":"telemetry/DC0021/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0063","name":"Windows Registry Key Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0063","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--da85d358-741a-410d-9433-20d6269a6170","page":"telemetry/DC0063/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0204","name":"Detection Strategy for T1547.010 – Port Monitor DLL Persistence via spoolsv.exe (Windows)","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0204","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--a62dbd10-5b61-489c-a465-8f792792778e","relationship_id":"relationship--c30dfb12-041c-49d3-bce4-a7de82917d1e"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0580","name":"Analytic 0580","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0204#AN0580","guidance":"Detects suspicious registry modifications under `HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Print\\Monitors\\*\\Driver`, DLL loads by `spoolsv.exe` of non-standard or unsigned modules, and abnormal usage of the `AddMonitor` API by non-installation processes. This pattern often indicates an attempt to persist a malicious DLL via the print monitor mechanism, particularly when correlated with creation of files in `C:\\Windows\\System32` not tied to known patches or installations.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0204"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0580","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0204#AN0580","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0016","component":"Module Load","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=7","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0580","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0204#AN0580","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"component_id":"DC0063","component":"Windows Registry Key Modification","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=13","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0580","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0204#AN0580","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated"